@strong{@anchor{Exercise 2.17}Exercise 2.17:} Define a procedure
@code{last_pair} that returns the list that contains only the last element of a
given (nonempty) list:

@example ocaml
last_pair [ 23; 72; 149; 34 ];;
(* => [34] *)
@end example
@end quotation

@quotation
@strong{@anchor{Exercise 2.18}Exercise 2.18:} Define a procedure @code{reverse}
that takes a list as argument and returns a list of the same elements in
reverse order:

@example ocaml
reverse [ 1; 4; 9; 16; 25 ];;
(* => [25; 16; 9; 4; 1] *)
@end example
