@noindent
We can produce balanced patterns by branching upwards as well as towards the
right (see @ref{Exercise 2.44}, @ref{Figure 2.13} and @ref{Figure 2.14}):

@example ocaml
let rec corner_split painter n =
  if n = 0
  then painter
  else
    let up = up_split painter (n - 1) in
    let right = right_split painter (n - 1) in
    let top_left = beside up up in
    let bottom_right = below right right in
    let corner = corner_split painter (n - 1) in
    beside (below painter top_left) (below bottom_right corner)
;;
@end example

@noindent
The @code{up_split} used here is @ref{Exercise 2.44}'s; the runnable module of
this section carries a definition so that @code{corner_split} compiles, exactly
as a Scheme session would carry one typed in from the exercise.

